{"findings":[{"id":"240d001d-da71-4e84-b2be-a93978491717","title":"Clock correction blocks later joins","description":"`s.push()` keeps advancing `latest` when a clock-sync update moves `s.now()` backward, so new pushes retain timestamps from before the correction. If a device taps before its first clock reply and its clock is ahead of the time keeper’s, subsequent taps can be too far ahead to pair with another device’s tap or can be silently rejected by the time keeper.","category":"Correctness","action_level":"action_required","attribution_status":"pending","git_sha":"696f15805d23e2c1a3bbc57e19abaa47b16a2240","location":{"file_path":"web/net.js","start_line":163,"end_line":163,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/net.js[21-29]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/net.js[63-73]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/net.js[100-108]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/net.js[160-165]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/layout.js[125-136]"}]}},{"id":"07c384af-9671-437a-83c4-3b427ff9f947","title":"A leader change hides a valid join result","description":"`fromLeader()` checks a result against the receiver’s current `s.leader`, rather than the leader that decided the push. If the old time keeper resolves a join between devices that remain in the room and then leaves before its `joined` broadcast arrives, those devices elect a successor and discard the in-flight result.","category":"Correctness","action_level":"remediation_recommended","attribution_status":"pending","git_sha":"1306dc9550075866fb556726e87e1526b70fe4b9","location":{"file_path":"web/net.js","start_line":150,"end_line":151,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/net.js[33-52]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/net.js[110-116]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/net.js[127-153]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"web/index.html[364-369]"}]}},{"id":"4bf90ebe-18fb-43ef-8cbe-b845d9227735","title":"Join tests skip non-facing and edge taps","description":"The new join checks in `tests/two-browser.mjs` and `tests/net.test.mjs` start every join through direct `net.push` calls, so no test sends a tap from a strip or a tap position. Non-facing taps, endpoint positions and default keyboard positions are never exercised. Strip-based stacking and overlap are deferred by the author's stated scope, so this is a known gap rather than a defect in the shipped path, but a later change could join ineligible taps without any failing check.","category":"Maintainability","action_level":"remediation_recommended","attribution_status":"dismissed","git_sha":"696f15805d23e2c1a3bbc57e19abaa47b16a2240","location":{"file_path":"tests/two-browser.mjs","start_line":68,"end_line":70,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"ticket","source":"https://github.com/jtbinith/qodo-hack-2026/issues/68"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"tests/two-browser.mjs[67-69]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"tests/net.test.mjs[59-72]"}]}}],"finding_state":{"complete":true,"introduced":["240d001d-da71-4e84-b2be-a93978491717"],"resolved":[],"still_open":["07c384af-9671-437a-83c4-3b427ff9f947"],"dismissed":["4bf90ebe-18fb-43ef-8cbe-b845d9227735"]},"review_agent_comment":"Nothing to comment.","meta":{"analysis":{"baseline_checkpoint_id":"df03d0c6838e408995e8d544fb8967dd","mode":"full","reason":"comparison_branch_unavailable"},"checkpoint":{"base_sha":"696f15805d23e2c1a3bbc57e19abaa47b16a2240","coverage_started_at":"2026-11-21T18:35:13.963247+00:00","created_at":"2026-11-21T18:35:13.963247+00:00","id":"61a3200a445d4b708dd35e5089ee215f","sequence":37160,"tree_sha":"30fe08d31ddce0a0bbaf2593c9d91c69599909d2","version":1},"context":{"author_notes":{"input_chars":2192,"max_tokens":16000,"offloaded":false,"original_tokens":531,"outcome":"inline","rendered_chars":2362},"ticket_bodies":[{"index":1,"input_chars":17421,"max_tokens